-- SessionRuntimeEvent(type='text_delta', data={'content': 
'**Change**\n\n`src/components/AsyncPanel.tsx`\n- Added an `attempt` counter 
that keys the existing simulation effect, so a retry re-runs the same 120 ms 
simulated delay (effect cleanup still clears the timer, so repeated activation 
cannot leave overlapping timers).\n- Added `handleRetry()`: sets state back to 
`\'loading\'` (renders `Checking service…` immediately) and increments `attempt`
— no page reload, no remount of surrounding page state, so the selected task is 
untouched.\n- Added a `Retry sync` button inside the existing `role="alert"` 
error block, with `type="button"`, styled via the existing `button.secondary` 
class. It exists only in the `error` render branch, so it is absent on the `/` 
success path and disappears as soon as retry is 
activated.\n\n`src/styles.css`\n- Added `.sync-retry { justify-self: start; 
margin-top: 8px; }` so the new button sits neatly in the existing error 
grid.\n\n**Commands run**\n- `verify_frontend` (fixed task check: `npm run 
verify:agent` → `tsc --noEmit && vite build`, then `playwright test`): exit 0, 
build succeeded, 6/6 public tests passed.\n\n**Remaining risks**\n- Retry always
re-reads `?sync=error` from the URL, so a retry on the error URL will land back 
on the error state after the delay (as required by the "same simulated delay" 
wording); the success transition is covered by the existing success path.\n- 
Assistive-tech behavior relies on the pre-existing `aria-live="polite"` region 
for announcing the retry result; no new live-region assertions were run, as this
workspace\'s public tests do not cover them.', 'aid': 0})
