-- SessionRuntimeEvent(type='text_delta', data={'content': "VERDICT: 
FAIL\n\n**Finding — High severity: Retry returns to error instead of success at 
`/?sync=error`.**\n\nAffected behavior: The acceptance criterion requires retry 
to show `Checking service…` immediately and then complete as `All changes are 
synced.` after the simulated delay. The diff instead re-runs the same effect, 
which re-reads `?sync=error`, so after 120 ms it sets state back to 
`'error'`.\n\nExact diff evidence:\n```tsx\nconst requested = new 
URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get('sync');\n...\nsetState(requested 
=== 'error' ? 'error' : 'success');\n...\n}, [attempt]);\n\nfunction 
handleRetry() {\n  setState('loading');\n  setAttempt((current) => current + 
1);\n}\n```\n\nBecause `attempt` only re-triggers the existing effect and the 
URL still contains `sync=error`, retry deterministically returns to `Sync 
failed`.\n\nReproduction:\n1. Open `/?sync=error`.\n2. Confirm the error state 
and `Retry sync`.\n3. Activate `Retry sync`.\n4. Observe `Checking service…` 
immediately.\n5. After the simulated delay, observe `Sync failed` again instead 
of `All changes are synced.`\n\nBounded fix: Make retry force the success result
while preserving the initial URL-driven error state. For example, track whether 
this run is a retry and set the result accordingly:\n```tsx\nconst isRetry = 
attempt > 0;\n...\nsetState(isRetry || requested !== 'error' ? 'success' : 
'error');\n```\nor store the initial query result in a ref and let 
`handleRetry()` trigger a success attempt. Keep the existing effect cleanup so 
timers remain non-overlapping.", 'aid': 1})
